Chamfers: a chamfer's guide is not deformed beyond a hundredth of its
distance (mitcad#263).

The case: a chamfer along a chain of edges joined tangentially whose
curvature jumps at the joints (a crease up a wall and on over the rim's
roundings). ChFi3d_PerformElSpine makes the guide C2 by removing knots
within up to a tenth of the guide's length; the guide then ran 0.03 to 0.08
off the edges along the wall, and a chamfer's contacts, at its distances
from the guide, moved with it (the chamfer's section along a straight wall
0.0012 mm^2 short of its triangle for a chamfer of 0.2). For a chamfer the
knots are removed only where the guide moves by a hundredth of the
chamfer's smallest distance at most (ChFi3d_ChamferGuideDeformation);
other blends are unchanged.

